WEBVTT

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:06.120
In the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit, amen.

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:13.320
The reading from the Sinaxadion for October 13th, on which we commemorate, the Holy

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:18.560
Marjorie Jacob of Hamatura.

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:25.960
The rock cut Hamatura Monastery in Kusbat Lebanon is a Greek Orthodox monastery belonging to

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:32.000
the Patriarchate of Antioch, and it's one of the oldest in the country.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:38.040
The monastery is dedicated to the Dormition of the Theotokos, the Mother of God, but it is

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:45.640
more widely known as Hamatura Monastery, which is the name of the mountain the monastery

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:47.840
is built in.

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:54.560
Late in the 13th century, at the monastery of the Dormition of the Theotokos on Hamatura,

00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:57.960
Saint Jacob began his ascetic life.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:05.280
Later, when the monastery was destroyed by the Mamelukas, he re-established monasticism

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:09.320
along the perimeter of the ruined monastery.

00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:16.240
In time he rebuilt the monastery, regenerating and giving renewed vigor to monastic life

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:18.080
in the area.

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:25.640
His spiritual briskness, vivacity and popularity among believers drew the attention of the

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:33.200
Mamelukas, who set their minds to stop his enthusiasm and determination and forced him

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:36.320
to convert to Islam.

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:40.840
He adamantly refused their relentless pressures.

00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:47.600
When the Mamelukas's horribly coercive attempts failed, they dragged Saint Jacob along with

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:54.840
a number of monks and laymen from Saint George's monastery, situated atop of Mount Hamatura

00:01:54.840 --> 00:02:01.840
to Tripoli, the capital of northern Lebanon, and handed him to the Wali ruler.

00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:06.160
For almost a year he endured tremendous tortures.

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:13.560
Nevertheless, he did not give in or renounce his faith, despite receiving both adulations

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:17.400
and threats from the Mamelukas.

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:24.080
Although intimidated by the uncompromising Saint Jacob and his persistence, finally, as

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:32.280
was their custom in punishing their enemies, on October 13, Saint Jacob was beheaded.

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:37.840
In addition, the Mamelukas burned his body to ensure the church would not give him an

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:44.600
honorable burial as a martyr, a burial befitting a saint.

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:51.760
Not long after his death, seeing his sufferings and steadfast faith, our Lord bestowed on him

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:59.400
everlasting crowns and graces, and today he shines as a martyr as much as he was a beacon

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:02.080
during his earthly life.

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:08.720
At this time, the church announced Saint Jacob's holiness and added him to her list of honored

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:13.600
martyr saints and prayed for his intercession.

00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:18.160
Our saint was almost forgotten in the course of history.

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:24.040
This was due to the severe sufferings of the church under various Muslim soltenates,

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:30.480
that both weakened Christian spiritual life and resulted in a noticeable drop of Christian

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:32.480
literacy.

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:38.240
Additionally, all manuscripts and information that could have been sent and translated

00:03:38.240 --> 00:03:43.720
abroad were either forgotten, lost, or destroyed.

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:51.000
However, recorded encounters by the monastery's pilgrims upon seeing visions of Saint Jacob

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:58.360
and many others who sensed his presence, affirmed and authenticated his sainthood.

00:03:58.360 --> 00:04:04.840
Glorifying the name of the Lord, Saint Jacob also healed many.

00:04:04.840 --> 00:04:10.680
Recently, a clear mention of Saint Jacob was discovered in a manuscript preserved at the

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:19.160
Balamand monastery, in a Yerantikon, a hagiography, or compilation of biographical short stories

00:04:19.160 --> 00:04:22.200
and lives of holy saints.

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:29.640
In a Balamand archival manuscript, numbered 149, it clearly indicates that the church commemorates

00:04:29.640 --> 00:04:33.240
his memory on October 13th.

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:40.080
The monastery of the Dormition of the Theotokos of Kuspa, Hamatura in Lebanon, commemorated

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:48.360
his memory for the first time on the 13th of October, in the year 2002, in an all-night

00:04:48.360 --> 00:04:50.360
prayer vigil.

00:04:50.360 --> 00:04:56.480
A number of priests, deacons, and believers participated on that memorable day.

00:04:56.480 --> 00:05:03.720
As the attendees chanted, Saint Jacob's divine service, prepared and edited by the monastery's

00:05:03.720 --> 00:05:06.200
monks.

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:11.760
Saint Jacob has always been present with the faithful, appearing to some and blessing

00:05:11.760 --> 00:05:18.520
them, healing others, and he has repeatedly been heard by monks and visitors chanting

00:05:18.520 --> 00:05:24.520
in the church, encouraging them to go deeper in their spiritual lives.

00:05:24.520 --> 00:05:31.200
He even asked a faithful woman once to inform the monks that he will show them his grave,

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:35.080
but they disregarded the subject.

00:05:35.080 --> 00:05:42.840
On July 3rd, in the year 2008, while renewing the church floor, human bones were found buried

00:05:42.840 --> 00:05:49.600
in the chapel, with a little grave containing two human skeletons, showing marks of torture

00:05:49.600 --> 00:05:56.320
and beating, some coagulated blood and some liquid blood on the skull.

00:05:56.320 --> 00:06:03.040
They also found a part of a three-year-old child's skull, with some of his bones and two

00:06:03.040 --> 00:06:05.760
other skeletons.

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:12.680
According to modern laboratory testing conducted by Najee Saebi, M.D., who specializes in

00:06:12.680 --> 00:06:18.240
legal medicine, they dated back 650 years.

00:06:18.240 --> 00:06:22.960
One of these last two skeletons shows mark of fire.

00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:28.960
He was also decapitated, and his second neck vertebrae was lost.

00:06:28.960 --> 00:06:35.120
But this implies, according to the criteria of the Balamond manuscripts, is that it is

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:42.080
Saint Jacob's skeleton, who was in his fifties when he was killed, his companion who was in

00:06:42.080 --> 00:06:50.120
his forties, and as for the rest of the skeletons, they date to 450 years ago.

00:06:50.120 --> 00:06:56.760
The monks of old considered these relics holy, since they did not bury them in common graves,

00:06:56.760 --> 00:07:04.760
but in the middle of the church, and in a hastened way as a result of pressures and persecutions.

00:07:04.760 --> 00:07:11.000
Under the holy altar were found some parts of a child's skull, therefore the monks considered

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:13.160
them martyrs.

00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:23.920
The church was re-consecrated on October 16, in the year 1894, because it was vandalized.

00:07:23.920 --> 00:07:30.360
Under the blessing Metropolitan George of Beavlos, Anjbo Tris, said the Orthodox can add

00:07:30.360 --> 00:07:36.800
to their prayers the phrase, the martyred father of Amatura, whose relics were found in the

00:07:36.800 --> 00:07:39.480
monastery chapel.

00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:46.040
In addition to Saint Jacob, they will be commemorated on July 3, the date of the finding

00:07:46.040 --> 00:07:47.880
of their holy relics.

00:07:48.360 --> 00:07:54.920
Today believers and pilgrims are constantly reporting his apparitions, miraculous healings,

00:07:54.920 --> 00:07:57.840
and other grace-filled deeds.

00:07:57.840 --> 00:08:03.440
All of this kindled the spiritual fervor to celebrate the memory of this saint and give

00:08:03.440 --> 00:08:10.320
praise to the Lord, while honoring Saint Jacob of Amatura, who is still living among us in

00:08:10.320 --> 00:08:19.400
his monastery, performing miraculous deeds, calls and visitations to believers.

00:08:19.400 --> 00:08:26.040
Through the prayers of our holy fathers, O Lord, Jesus Christ our God, have mercy on us

00:08:26.040 --> 00:08:27.280
and save us.
